<p>Israeli strikes in southern Lebanon killed six people on Saturday, according to Lebanon’s health ministry, after Israel said rockets were launched from لبنان and accused Hezbollah of violating a recently extended ceasefire. Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu then ordered the army to strike Hezbollah targets “vigorously” or “forcefully,” and Lebanese state media later reported more raids and shelling. The Israeli military said some of those targeted were Hezbollah operatives, including people in a vehicle allegedly carrying weapons and another person on a motorcycle, while Hezbollah said it targeted an Israeli army vehicle in retaliation for one of the strikes. The flare-up showed how fragile the truce remains, even after President Trump announced on Thursday that the 10-day ceasefire that began on April 17 had been extended by three weeks, keeping hopes for calm alive but clearly under strain.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/__C2a_INDnfER_bgZ0QxsgrIZBowfNFqmyFMTv6xKsAnnPAwOUPlnIFN35Zi4wdtAE01_ictFSSeKDzLVP0J6fp6P3hhdeot3_VKZY2HfaQ7' alt='Israeli tanks and military vehicles move near destroyed houses in southern Lebanon close to the Israel border on April 25, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Strike locations: Lebanon’s health ministry said two strikes in Yohmor al-Shaqeef in Nabatieh district killed four people, while another airstrike on Safad al-Battikh in Bint Jbeil district killed two and wounded 17.</li><li>Israeli account: The Israeli military said it had “eliminated” more than 15 militants in southern Lebanon earlier, and said some of the latest targets were Hezbollah operatives, including people in a vehicle allegedly carrying weapons and another person on a motorcycle.</li><li>Cross-border fire: Israel said it detected two projectiles launched from Lebanon and later intercepted another “suspicious aerial target,” calling the launches a breach of the ceasefire terms.</li></ul><blockquote>A blatant violation of the ceasefire understandings - Israeli military</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli government: Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu told the military to attack Hezbollah targets vigorously after the army reported rocket launches from Lebanon and alleged truce violations. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yv1nvd4gjo'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>Lebanese authorities: Lebanon’s health ministry reported civilian deaths and injuries from the strikes, while state media documented more shelling and raids across southern areas. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995090/six-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-lebanon'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Hezbollah: Hezbollah said it targeted an Israeli army vehicle in south Lebanon in retaliation for the attack on Yohmor al-Shaqeef. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995090/six-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-lebanon'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>United States: President Trump announced on Thursday that the ceasefire that began on April 17 had been extended for three more weeks, signaling continued US backing for de-escalation efforts despite the renewed violence. (<a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/israel-says-it-will-attack-hezbollah-%27forcefully%27-as-four-killed-in-strikes-on-southern-lebanon'>Japan Today</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/04/26/israeli-strikes-kill-six-in-south-lebanon-despite-extended-ceasefire-fresh-raids-reported_6752834_4.html'>Israeli strikes kill six in south Lebanon despite extended ceasefire, fresh raids reported</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c5yv1nvd4gjo'>Netanyahu orders army to &#x27;vigorously attack&#x27; Hezbollah in Lebanon</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3351445/new-israeli-strikes-reported-lebanon-after-netanyahu-orders-attacks'>New Israeli strikes reported in Lebanon after Netanyahu orders attacks</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/wo